<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>Winter's Coming: When an AWD Rental Is Worth It (and When It Isn't)</h1>
<p>One all-wheel-drive Outback, two Ford Edge SUVs, and a Wisconsin winter on the way. Here's how to pick.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>First frost is here, and it won't be long before the first real snow on Highway 54. Every year that's when the calls change from "what's the cheapest car?" to "do you have anything with all-wheel drive?" The answer is yes &mdash; but only one, so here's how to decide whether you need it.</p>
<h2>What's in the class</h2>
<p>Our <a href="/suv-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">SUV &amp; AWD class</a> is two Ford Edge SUVs and one all-wheel-drive Subaru Outback. Rates are the same across the class:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>$80/day</strong> local (100 miles/day included) or <strong>$100/day</strong> unlimited</li>
<li><strong>$480/week</strong> local or <strong>$600/week</strong> unlimited</li>
</ul>
<p>If AWD specifically matters to you, ask for the Outback by name when you book.</p>
<h2>When AWD is worth it</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Unplowed or gravel roads:</strong> hunting land, cabins, and farm driveways that don't see a plow first.</li>
<li><strong>Early-morning highway runs</strong> after overnight snow, before crews have been through.</li>
<li><strong>Long trips with uncertain weather</strong> &mdash; a holiday drive to the Twin Cities or Madison when the forecast is iffy.</li>
<li><strong>Peace of mind</strong> for a visiting family member who isn't used to Wisconsin winters.</li>
</ul>
<h2>When a car is still smarter</h2>
<p>For plowed town driving and the interstate on a clear day, a <a href="/fleet" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">full-size car</a> at $65/day with good tires handles winter fine and saves you money. AWD helps you get going; it doesn't help you stop. Slow down either way.</p>
<h2>Why to book early</h2>
<p>There's one AWD Outback. Once the first storm hits the forecast, it goes fast &mdash; and deer season and Thanksgiving week stack on top of each other in late November. If you know you'll want AWD for a specific week, call now.</p>
<h2>Long winter stretch?</h2>
<p>Car in the shop after a deer strike or a slide-off? We handle <a href="insurance-replacement-rental-cars-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">insurance replacement rentals</a> all winter, and every weekly rental includes unlimited miles on the unlimited rate. <strong>Call or text 715-396-1466.</strong></p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Can I rent an AWD vehicle in Black River Falls?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Our SUV/AWD class includes an all-wheel-drive Subaru Outback. Ask for it by name when you book, since there's one in the fleet.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">How much is an SUV or AWD rental for winter?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>$80/day local (100 miles/day) or $100/day unlimited; $480/week local or $600/week unlimited.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Do I need AWD for winter driving in Wisconsin?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Not always. For plowed roads and clear interstate days, a car with good tires works fine. AWD helps most on unplowed, gravel, or rural roads and after fresh snow.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">When should I book an AWD rental for the holidays?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>As early as possible. Deer season and Thanksgiving week overlap in late November, and there's only one AWD Outback.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:48px;padding-top:32px;border-top:1px solid var(--light-gray);">
